# page-diff (matching-a-page skill) local output.
#
# The WORKSPACE is ignored — ~2.0GB of downloaded reference HTML/CSS, gate
# screenshots and out-*/ runs — but the SCRIPTS and RECORDS are tracked (~2.4MB):
#   • CLAUDE.md's rules tell every future session to run matching/gate.sh,
#     matching/strikes.mjs and matching/next.mjs. Ignoring them left those rules
#     pointing at files that do not exist on a fresh clone.
#   • matching/LEDGER.md is the audit trail for every operator decision on this
#     rebuild (the AA ACK, the "Book an Appointment" spelling, the dead-buttons
#     call). It existed in exactly one unbacked place.
#   • matching/SPEC.md + spec-sections/ are Phase 1's output, which Phase 4
#     refuses to run without.
scratch-diff*/
matching/*
!matching/*.sh
!matching/*.mjs
!matching/*.md
!matching/spec-sections/
!matching/states/
matching/states/*
!matching/states/*.mjs
# derived artefacts, even where the extensions above would catch them
matching/*.log
matching/*.json
matching/*.png
